        "378ba365e7d1…242066ef",
        "Verify tx →"
      ],
      "text": "Tachi hackathon · Bounty #6 · x402 on Bitcoin Pay-per-request, in native sats. No accounts. No API keys. No custodian. Sats402 is the SDK and protocol that enables autonomous AI agents to make pay-per-request micropayments using native sats on Tachi. An agent pays for each call by signing its own transaction; the service verifies by reading the chain. Settlement is committed on-chain in about 5.5s (Tachi consensus finality). The HTTP round-trip is what the agent sees. Run a real payment → Browse services → Verify a settlement → LIVE RECEIPT · TACHI SETTLEMENT committed 50 sats agent-to-agent T",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "div",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 875,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 266,
      "heading": "Four live services, priced in sats, each one runnable.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
      "callsToAction": [
        "Run a real payment →"
      ],
      "text": "Live services & demo Four live services, priced in sats, each one runnable. Run a real payment → 1. Challenge (402) Service issues price in sats and payee key on first request. 2. Settlement (tachi_tx) Agent validates policy, signs, and broadcasts native sats transaction. 3. Delivery (200) Service verifies daemon settlement and delivers response with receipt.",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "div",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1141,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 374,
      "heading": "Built for the agent economy, on Bitcoin",
      "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
      "callsToAction": [
        "verify page"
      ],
      "text": "Built for the agent economy, on Bitcoin Sats402 is the x402 exact scheme on Tachi: the wire format the standard defines, settled as a Tachi transaction. The money moves exactly once, and the proof of payment is a transaction id anyone can check. FOR AGENTS A spending policy is part of the SDK Per-call cap, session budget, payee allowlist. A call that breaks policy is refused locally, before any transaction exists. FOR SERVICES One middleware, zero custody Drop the paywall in front of any handler. It issues the challenge and verifies payment by reading the chain. It never holds a key. FOR EVERY",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    }
